course: dictionary
lesson: 12483
title: Deliverance: being rescued and set free
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Deliverance means being rescued or set free from danger, suffering or evil. It is a formal word, so you will meet it more in serious stories, speeches and old hymns than in everyday talk. When you meet it, ask yourself: what was the danger, and who or what set the people free?
explain: «The villagers prayed for deliverance when the flood water rose.» The prayer tells you the villagers were in danger and wanted rescue. Swap in the meaning: "The villagers prayed for being rescued from danger" still makes sense, so deliverance means rescue.
explain: In Bible stories, deliverance often means God saving people. «God brought deliverance to the Israelites when they were slaves in Egypt.» The clues are slaves and Egypt: the people were held in slavery, and God set them free.
explain: Adventure stories use the word too, for the moment a hero is finally rescued after a long danger. Look for phrases like «a day of deliverance» or «deliverance from slavery», which show that something frightening has come to an end.
fact: Deliverance is an uncountable noun, so we do not usually say "a deliverance" or "two deliverances".
fact: «Deliverance» means being rescued or set free from danger, suffering or evil.
fact: In Christian and Jewish teaching, deliverance means God saving people, as when God led the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt.
fact: Christians pray «deliver us from evil»: the verb is deliver, and the noun is deliverance.
fact: Deliverance is a formal word, so you will find it in serious stories, hymns and speeches.
exercise: «The villagers prayed for deliverance when the flood water rose.» What does deliverance mean here? | Going on a long trip | A big feast after the harvest | Being given a new coat | *Being rescued from danger
exercise: «God brought deliverance to the Israelites in Egypt.» What kind of help was this? | A holiday at the seaside | Learning to read and write | Getting a new house | *Being set free from slavery
exercise: «The prisoners waited for years, and at last came the day of deliverance.» What was the day of deliverance? | *The day they were set free | A big meal in the prison yard | The day the prison walls were painted | The day they were sent to prison
test: «After the storm, the sailors finally saw the lighthouse and knew their deliverance was near.» What does deliverance mean? | Being sent out to sea on a new ship | Sailing in a race | Losing their map in the fog | *Being rescued from the storm
test: Which sentence uses deliverance correctly? | *The firefighters brought deliverance to the family trapped in the burning house | We walked to deliverance on Monday | The deliverance was painted bright blue | Ella ate a deliverance of toast for breakfast
exam: Which phrase is most like deliverance from slavery in the Bible? | Sleeping in a tent on a camping trip | *Being freed from being forced to work as a slave | Learning a new song for school | Painting a picture of the sea
